     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Answers on getting the probabilities of ancestral states/ranges, and getting the labels of ancestral states/ranges:<div>\r\n<br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\" style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80)\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">\r\n<div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br><br>On Fri, Feb 14, 2014 at 10:47 AM, X wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div>\r\nHi Nick!<br><br>I hope all is well! I just have a quick question about BioGeoBEARS. Is there a function to use to get a list of the inferred ancestral range at each node, as in presence/absence in the regions specified? I think I recall you mentioning such a function during the workshop in Canberra... Thank you!<br>\r\n\r\n<br>All the best,<br></div>X</blockquote></div><br></div></blockquote></div><div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><div><font color=\"#888888\"><br><div></div></font></div><div><br>On Feb 14, 2014, at 8:56 AM, Nick Matzke &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mat...@nimbios.org</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></div>\r\n\r\n<div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Howdy!  Yeah, it&#39;s easy:<div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/biogeobears/LlbN1jW8w5E\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/biogeobears/LlbN1jW8w5E&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485691176000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Nqly_zPHLsct_pC0IEBhE\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/biogeobears/LlbN1jW8w5E</a><br>\r\n\r\n</div><div>=======================</div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">You can see the node numbers with... </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">=========== </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">plot(tr, show.tip.label=FALSE) </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">nodelabels() </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">tiplabels() </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">=========== </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Or to print a nice table, use the BioGeoBEARS function prt: </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">=========== </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">prt(tr) </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">=========== </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Ancestral state probabilities in a BioGeoBEARS results </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">object, like resDEC are stored in: </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">resDEC$ML_marginal_prob_each_</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">state_at_branch_top_AT_node </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">The rows are node numbers, the columns are the different </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">states=ranges. </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">The other big tables in res are pieces of the calculation of </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">the ancestral probs, or the overall data likelihood. </span><br style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n</div><div>=======================</div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\" style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\" style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80)\">\r\n<br></div>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_extra\" style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80)\">On Fri, Feb 14, 2014 at 12:54 PM, X wrote:<div><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><div>Hello again! </div><div><br></div><div>Just one thing I&#39;m still confused about the columns which indicate the different ranges in the <span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">resDEC$ML_marginal_prob_each_</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">state_at_branch_top_AT_node object... Is there a way to check what region combinations correspond to each column? </span><br>\r\n\r\n<br>Thanks! </div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div><div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">---------- Forwarded message ----------<br>From: <b class=\"gmail_sendername\">Nick Matzke</b> <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mat...@nimbios.org</a>&gt;</span><br>\r\n\r\nDate: Fri, Feb 14, 2014 at 1:27 PM<br>Subject: Re: Inferred node ranges?<br>To: X<br><br><br><div dir=\"ltr\">So, this code should do it:<div><br></div><div><div>================================</div><div># Get the areas</div>\r\n\r\n<div>tipranges = tipranges = getranges_from_LagrangePHYLIP(lgdata_fn=np(res$inputs$geogfn))</div>\r\n<div>tipranges</div><div>areas = getareas_from_tipranges_object(tipranges)</div><div>areas</div><div>state_indices_0based = rcpp_areas_list_to_states_list(areas=areas, maxareas=res$inputs$max_range_size, include_null_range=TRUE)</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>state_indices_0based</div><div><br></div><div># Get the ranges</div><div>ranges_list = areas_list_to_states_list_new(areas=areas, maxareas=length(areas),</div><div>include_null_range=TRUE, split_ABC=FALSE)</div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\nranges_list</div><div>ranges = unlist(ranges_list)</div><div>ranges</div></div><div>================================</div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>\r\n<br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
